= {!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Allahyar Saleh{!</span>!}

{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Saleh{!</span>!} is an
{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Iran Party{!</span>!} organizer
who becomes a {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}National Front{!</span>!}
figure. His own Kashan/Natanz credential passed during the Sixteenth
{!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!}. The consultation abstracts
electoral reporting and durable organization rather than presenting a complete
personal portfolio.

- @saleh_reports
- @saleh_committee
- @saleh_credentials
- @main: Return to the monthly briefing

@saleh_reports
title: Audit constituency reports
subtitle: <span class="term term-constitutionalist">Saleh</span> separates claims that can survive a credential hearing from rumor that cannot
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and front_formed = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if front_formed = 0: Available after the common electoral protest. ?][? if front_formed = 1: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before another adviser action. ?]
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 4; organizational_reach += 2

{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Saleh{!</span>!} reviews constituency reports against the coalition's register and asks
organizers to label observation, hearsay, and missing evidence separately.
Uncertain returns remain uncertain.

The secretariat gains a record it can use in credential petitions without
overstating uncertain evidence.

- @main: Return to the monthly briefing

@saleh_committee
title: Strengthen local committees
subtitle: Local <span class="term term-constitutionalist">Iran Party</span> committees collect complaints, names, and returns in a common form
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and front_formed = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if front_formed = 0: Available after the common electoral protest. ?][? if front_formed = 1: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before another adviser action. ?]
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; organizational_reach += 4; iran_party_organization += 3

{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Saleh{!</span>!} works through
{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Iran Party{!</span>!} contacts
to standardize meeting records,
membership follow-up, and reports to the secretariat. The committees remain
locally rooted while becoming easier to connect to a national campaign.

The {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} reaches
farther and receives more regular information. This route
strengthens one component's machinery more than the others.

- @main: Return to the monthly briefing

@saleh_credentials
title: Prepare a model credential file
subtitle: One exemplary file becomes a model other deputies can carry into the chamber
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and majles_convened = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if majles_convened = 0: Available when the Sixteenth {!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!} convenes. ?][? if majles_convened = 1: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before another adviser action. ?]
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 4; mossadegh_authority += 1; iran_party_relation += 2

{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Saleh{!</span>!} assembles one complete file that distinguishes the return, the credential
decision, and the point at which a deputy becomes usable in the chamber. The
format gives other organizers a standard they can copy.

The credential campaign becomes more disciplined and
{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Iran Party{!</span>!} cooperation
improves. One model cannot resolve every disputed place.

- @main: Return to the monthly briefing
